MANUAL_BOOK_C = {
    "10.17": {'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.17 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021); Alta.*' then a line break and 'Reg. 36/2020, s. 13 effective May 26,  (Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)] (Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)]': the year after 'May 26,' is lost and the Gazette entry '(Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)]' is printed twice (as in the 10.13 and 10.15 notes). The regulation numbers and section number agree with the official history (AR 124/2010; 36/2020) and with Book B ('Alta. Reg. 36/2020, s. 13'); the Gazette dates and 'effective May 26' are not in the official text and were not checked. The rule text of Book C's entry equals the official text.", 'commentary_flag': "(1) The commentary ('General Principles', 238 characters, no citation) is cut off: 'The authority under rule 10.17(1)(b) to direct the production of records is intended to empower the review officer to order production, and not to preclude the court' is followed by the page's running head 'PART 10 LAWYERS' CHARGES, RECOVERABLE COSTS OF LITIGATION, AND SANCTIONS' and no more. What is printed is consistent with official 10.17(1)(b) ('direct the production of records'); neither Book A nor Book B has a matching passage (Book B's commentary is the Sonnenberg guidelines for reviewing contingency accounts), and the case it comes from is not named. The passage is kept as printed (flagged)."},
    "10.16": {'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.16 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021)]*': 'Alta. Reg. 124/2010' and 'November 1, 2010' agree with the official history (AR 124/2010, no amending regulation); the Gazette date is the one Book C prints throughout Part 10 (see the 10.1 flag) and was not checked. Book C's entry has the rule text (equal to the official text), no commentary and no citation."},
    "10.15": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): it ends '(ii) a review officer, or R. 10.15' - subparagraph (iii) 'the Court.' is missing and 'R. 10.15' (the page's running head) stands in its place; the words before that equal the official text.", 'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.15 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021); Alta.' then a line break and 'Reg. 140/2013, s. 11; Alta. Reg. 36/2020, s. 12 effective May 26,  (Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)] (Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)]': the year after 'May 26,' is lost and the Gazette entry '(Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)]' is printed twice (as in the 10.13 note). The regulation numbers and section numbers agree with the official history (AR 124/2010; 140/2013; 36/2020) and with Book B; the Gazette dates and 'effective May 26' are not in the official text and were not checked. Book C's entry has no commentary or citation."},
    "10.14": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): subrule (1) is cut off after '(a) a copy of the account, appropriately signed, in respect of which the client seeks a review,' so paragraphs (b) and (c) are missing; subrules (2) and (3) equal the official words.", 'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.14 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021); Alta.*' then a line break and 'Reg. 140/2013, s. 10; Alta. Reg. 128/2015, s. 9; Alta. Reg. 36/2020, s. 11 effective May 26,' and stops: the year and the closing Gazette entry are cut off (the 10.13 note prints '(Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)' twice). The regulation numbers and section numbers agree with the official history (AR 124/2010; 140/2013; 128/2015; 36/2020) and with Book B; the Gazette dates and 'effective May 26' are not in the official text and were not checked.", 'commentary_flag': "(1) The commentary ('General Principles', 1,212 characters) is cut off at 'on' (the last sentence, 'A lawyer's contravention of rule 10.14 could be a sufficient basis on which to deny costs and require payment to the former client costs for appearances before the review officer and on', has no end). The first paragraph agrees with Book A's note (a short adjournment; the forfeiture in subrule (3) is not mechanical), which cites the same case, Moore v. Hildebrand 2013 ABQB 167; the words 'the review officer should consider whether a short adjournment would remedy the issue.An adjournment could be as short as a few minutes' have no space after the full stop (as printed). The second paragraph ('The foundational rules (Part 1) cannot override the specific requirement in rule 10.14 to file a retainer agreement', Moore para 16; 'The quickest way at the least expense for the review officer to get background context ... is to examine, before the review hearing, the basic materials, including the retainer agreement', Moore para 17) is consistent with official 10.14(1)(c) (a copy of any retainer agreement, 'whether or not the lawyer intends to rely on' it); the paragraph pinpoints (paras 22, 16 and 17) are not checked against Moore, which neither Book A nor Book B quotes. The passage is kept as printed (flagged)."},
    "10.13": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): subrule (1) is cut off after 'A lawyer or a client may, by request,' so 'obtain from a review officer an appointment date for a review of a retainer agreement or a lawyer's charges, or both' is missing; the words of subrules (2)-(5) equal the official text.", 'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.13 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021); Alta.*' then a line break and 'Reg. 140/2013, s. 9; Alta. Reg. 36/2020, s. 10 effective May 26,  (Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)] (Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)]': the year after 'May 26,' is lost (the 10.10 note prints 'effective May 26, 2020') and the Gazette entry '(Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)]' is printed twice. 'Alta. Reg. 124/2010', 'Alta. Reg. 140/2013, s. 9' and 'Alta. Reg. 36/2020, s. 10' agree with the official history (AR 124/2010; 140/2013; 36/2020) and with Book B; the Gazette dates and 'effective May 26' are not in the official text and were not checked.", 'citation_names': {'2013 ABQB 748': 'Treasury Branches v. 1401057 Alberta Ltd (c.o.b. Katch 22)'}, 'citation_notes': {'2020 ABQB 85': "Printed 'Fleming v. Fleming Alberta , [2020] A.J. No. 142, 2020 ABQB 85 at paras. 26-30': the name is garbled (see the 10.11 note) and the case is cited in no other file of the packet.", '2013 ABQB 748': "Printed 'Treasury Branches v. 1401057 Alberta Ltd (c.o.b. Katch 22) . , [2013] A.J. No. 1449, 2013 ABQB 748 at footnote 3': Book A prints '1401057 Alta.' and Book B '14010507 Alberta Ltd (Katch 22)' (see the 10.11 note)."}, 'commentary_flag': '(1) The commentary (\'General Principles\', 809 characters) is cut off after the words \'Alberta Rules of Court\' (no closing sentence). \'Rules 10.9 and 10.13(1) bestow on a client the right to ask a review officer to assess the reasonableness of a retainer agreement. Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs LLP, [2014] A.J. No. 62, 2014 ABQB 34 at footnote 10\': agrees with the rules (official 10.13(1) lets a client obtain an appointment for a review of a retainer agreement; 10.9 makes retainer agreements reviewable) and with Book B\'s 10.9 commentary (Steinke para 51 carries footnote marker \'10\' after \'retainer agreement\'; the text of that footnote is not printed in Book B, and neither Book A nor Book B cites \'10.13(1)\' for it). \'A court must hold the lawyer and the client to promises made in a retainer agreement. Steinke ... at para. 51\' agrees with Book B (para 51: \'The third principle is that a court must hold the lawyer and the client to promises made in a retainer agreement ... in the absence of a compelling reason not to\'). \'A "client" includes "a person who is or may be liable to pay or who has paid lawyer\'s charges or part of them"\' agrees with the Appendix definition (official line 40619); the Fleming (paras 26-30), Katch 22 and \'definitions (contained in an appendix to those rules)\' citations are the same as in the 10.11 commentary and are not tied to the appointment procedure of 10.13. Nothing in the passage is about the filing and service steps of subrules (2)-(5), and Book B\'s commentary (Legal Aid lawyers and old R. 630) is not in Book C. The passage is kept as printed (flagged).'},
    "10.12": {'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.12 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021)]*': 'Alta. Reg. 124/2010' and 'November 1, 2010' agree with the official history (AR 124/2010, no amending regulation); the Gazette date is the one Book C prints throughout Part 10 (see the 10.1 flag) and was not checked. Book C's entry has the rule text (equal to the official text) and no commentary or citation."},
    "10.11": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): it ends after '(vi) the retainer agreement between the lawyer and the client so provides, and' and the amendment note, so paragraph (b) (subparagraphs (i)-(iv), the lawyer's requests) is missing; what is printed equals the official words except the hyphenated 'proceed- ings'.", 'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.11 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021)]': 'Alta. Reg. 124/2010' and 'November 1, 2010' agree with the official history (AR 124/2010, no amending regulation); the Gazette date is the one Book C prints throughout Part 10 (see the 10.1 flag) and was not checked.", 'citation_names': {'2013 ABQB 748': 'Treasury Branches v. 1401057 Alberta Ltd (c.o.b. Katch 22)'}, 'citation_notes': {'2020 ABQB 85': "Printed 'Fleming v. Fleming Alberta , [2020] A.J. No. 142, 2020 ABQB 85 at para. 26': the name is garbled (the word 'Alberta' follows the second Fleming) and the case is cited in no other file of the packet.", '2013 ABQB 748': "Printed 'Treasury Branches v. 1401057 Alberta Ltd (c.o.b. Katch 22) . , [2013] A.J. No. 1449, 2013 ABQB 748 at footnote 3': Book A (p.10-124 fn 1 and later notes) prints 'Alta. Treas. Br. v.1401057 Alta.2013 ABQB 748, 579 AR 152' and Book B prints 'Alberta Treasury Branches v. 14010507 Alberta Ltd (Katch 22)'; the number of the company differs (1401057 against 14010507)."}, 'commentary_flag': '(1) The commentary (\'General Principles\', 1,417 characters) is cut off and holds a passage that is not about who may request a review. (a) \'The review process is available as between lawyers and clients ... Borden Ladner Gervais LLP v. CBI Investments Ltd., [2015] A.J. No. 782, 2015 ABQB 442 at para. 8 (Alta. Q.B.), affd [2016] A.J. No. 388, 2016 ABQB 220\': the 2016 decision is cited in Book A\'s 10.5 note (p.10-13, line 591) and 10.13 note (p.10-29, line 1424) as \'Borden Ladner & Co. v. CBI Invs. 2016 ABQB 220, 89 CPC(7th) 399\'; 2015 ABQB 442 is cited nowhere else in the packet. (b) \'The term "client" as used in this rule could mean any person to whom a lawyer has rendered an account for lawyer\'s charges, and a person who is or may be liable to pay or who has paid lawyer\'s charges or part of them\' agrees with the Appendix definition of \'client\' (official line 40619); the paragraph ends \'and definitions (contained in an appendix to those rules).\' (c) The words \'Alberta Rules of Court The assessment process is effectively a modified trial process. Parties are heard, evidence is tendered, and a decision is made by an unbiased party. The assessment process is a release valve that serves both the legal profession and the community. Matters that would otherwise burden an over-worked judicial system are funnelled directly to an expert adjudicator ... It is a tool with tangible benefits for\' follow with no citation: the passage is cut off at \'for\' and is about the assessment process (assessment of costs, Division 2), not the review of lawyers\' charges; it appears in no other Book C entry (searched for \'modified trial process\' in the four Part 10 Book C files: one entry, 10.11) and in no Book A or Book B file. The passage is kept as printed (flagged); its source is not identified in the packet.'},
    "10.10": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): in subrule (1) the number '6' is lost and a citation stands in its place ('if  Willier v. McGurk, [2015] A.J. No. 1011, 2015 ABCA 299 at para. 12 (Alta. C.A.). months has passed'); the words of subrule (2) equal the official text.", 'drop_citations': "The one rule-level citation (Willier v. McGurk, [2015] A.J. No. 1011, 2015 ABCA 299 at para. 12 (Alta. C.A.)) stands where the '6' is lost in 10.10(1); it is not an authority for 10.10 as printed here. The same case is cited elsewhere in the packet for permission to appeal (Book B rule10_part10_document.json '... Willier v McGurk, 2015 ABCA 299 (CanLII) at para 8' and rule14_part01_document.json 'In Willier v. McGurk, 2015 ABCA 299, Justice Veldhuis said: 6 The factors to be considered on permission to appeal applications under the former Rules...'); the case is not cited in the Part 10 Book A file or in Book B's 10.10 commentary.", 'citation_names': {'2019 ABQB 949': 'Rath and Co. Barristers and Solicitors v. Sturgeon Lake Cree Nation', '2012 ABQB 44': 'Twinn v. Sawridge Band', '2015 ABQB 535': "O'Brien v. de Villars Jones", '2013 ABQB 350': "Samson Cree Nation v. O'Reilly & Associés", '2014 ABCA 268': "Samson Cree Nation v. O'Reilly & Associés", '2014 ABQB 34': 'Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs LLP', '2017 ABQB 339': 'Eryn B. Logie Family Law v. West', '2018 ABCA 255': 'Eryn B. Logie Family Law v. West'}, 'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.10 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021); Alta.*' then a line break and 'Reg. 140/2013, s. 8; Alta. Reg. 36/2020, s.  Law Society of Alberta Code of Conduct (February 20, 2020), s. 3.6-1. effective May 26, 2020 (Alta. Gaz. April 15, 2020)]'. The section number after 'Alta. Reg. 36/2020, s.' is lost and a citation to the Law Society of Alberta Code of Conduct (February 20, 2020), s. 3.6-1 stands in its place (Book B's note reads 'Alta. Reg. 140/2013, s. 8; 36/2020, s. 9'); the Code citation is not part of the regulation history. 'Alta. Reg. 124/2010' and 'November 1, 2010' agree with the official history (AR 124/2010; 140/2013; 36/2020); the Gazette dates 'May 15, 2021' (see the 10.1 flag) and 'April 15, 2020', and 'effective May 26, 2020', are not in the official text and were not checked.", 'commentary_flag': '(1) The commentary (\'General Principles\', 2,433 characters, no topic other than that heading) is one run of text with citations displaced by lost characters. (a) The list of purposes: bullets 2-4 (put lawyers on notice; encourage clients to voice concerns close to the date; allow lawyers to anticipate uncollectible receivables) correspond to West v. Logie 2018 ABCA 255 para 22 as quoted in Book B\'s 10.10 commentary, which cites Twinn para 38; bullet 1 (\'give the client a fair opportunity\'), bullet 5 (\'allow lawyers to have finality of accounts\'), the clause \'which allows both parties to retain records and make notes\' and the clause \'or to know that collected accounts may have to be returned\' are not in Book B\'s excerpt of para 22. The last bullet is followed by \'Rath and Co. ... v. Sturgeon Lake Cree Nation, [2019] A.J. No. 1688, 2019 ABQB 949 at para. 16 (Alta. Q.B. (Master)), revd on other grounds [2022] A.J. No. 996, 2022 ABQB\' where the number after \'ABQB\' is lost (Book A p.10-26 fn 6 and Book B give 2022 ABQB 556 for the decision of Justice Johnston, JCC 1801 11136 in Book A) and the sentence \'The former version of this rule only applied to client-initiated reviews. Twinn v. Sawridge Band, [2012] A.J. No. 59, 2012 ABQB 44 at paras. 34-40\' follows in its place; Twinn paras 38 (Book B part 3) and 36-37 (Book B\'s 10.24 commentary) fall inside the printed range. (b) \'The words "whether at the request of the lawyer or the client" were added to the rule on July 25, 2013\' agrees with Book B (O\'Brien para 6). \'Lawyers are now bound by the rule. O\'Brien v. de Villars Jones ... 2015 ABQB 535 at para. 6\': Book B\'s excerpt has \'lawyers are now bound by the six month term\' in para 7 (para 6 has the date); the pinpoint is printed as is. \'The rule does not apply to interim invoices, only final invoices. O\'Brien ... at para. 8\': para 8 is not in Book B\'s excerpt (paras 4-7 and 21-25); Book A\'s 10.2 note (p.10-4 fn 5, lines 134-137) has \'then the bills rendered were final; nothing in R.10.2 would apply: O\'Brian v. de Villars Jones\' and Book A\'s 10.10 note says \'The time limits probably do not apply to interim accounts\'. \'For whether an account is interim or final, see , [2013] A.J. Samson Cree Nation v. O\'Reilly & Associés No. 670, 2013 ABQB 350 at paras. 45, 46\' has the case name displaced into the middle of its own citation; the pinpoint lands (Book B\'s Samson Cree quotation prints para 45 \'Periodic accounts may be interim or final\' and para 46 \'Final accounts are ones that...\'). (c) \'The time limit seeks to make it easier to resolve disputes by avoiding the difficulty of assessing complaints about events years past, puts lawyers on notice ... and allows PART  Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs LLP, [2014] A.J. No. 62, 2014 ABQB 34 at para. 50\' stops at \'and allows\' and the page\'s running head \'PART\' (from \'PART 10 LAWYERS\' CHARGES, RECOVERABLE COSTS OF LITIGATION, AND SANCTIONS\') and the Steinke citation follow; the same list is in West v. Logie para 22 (Book B), which cites Twinn para 38; Book A\'s Part 10 file cites Steinke at paras 53, 63-4, 65, 93, 96, 51, 54, 47-48, 72 and 8-24 and not para 50 (the pinpoint is printed as is). (d) The last paragraph (\'13.5(2), Eryn B. Logie Family Law v. West, [2017] A.J. No. 525, 2017 ABQB 339 at para. 12 (Alta. Q.B.), revd [2018] A.J. No. 888, 2018 ABCA 255 (Alta. C.A.); , Samson Cree Nation v. O\'Reilly & Associés which is not excluded by rule 10.10.98 Factors to be considered for extending time are: i. delay, ii. prejudice, iii. first intent to tax (assess the accounts), [2014] A.J. No. 904, 2014 ABCA 268 at para. 184 (Alta. C.A.)\') begins in the middle of a sentence (\'13.5(2)\' is the rule that lets the Court extend time), has \'98\' run onto \'10.10.\' (a footnote number), is cut off after the third factor, and prints the Samson Cree 2014 ABCA 268 citation where the list should continue. Book B\'s Attila Dogan 2015 ABQB 407 para 33 lists six factors (delay, prejudice, first intent to tax, evidence of overcharging, agreement as to amount, relationship between lawyer and client) and Book A says \'case law gives 4 or 6 factors\'. Book B\'s West v. Logie excerpt (paras 19-23) rejects the chambers judge\'s \'low threshold\' for extending time; Book A p.10-25 fn 9 cites West v. Logie (paras 20-26) for the same. The passage is kept as printed (flagged); nothing in it contradicts the official 10.10(2), which Book C\'s rule text repeats (\'one year\').'},
    "10.9": {'commentary_flag': "(1) Rule text equals the official text (EXACT_MATCH); the amendment note is in the standard form (see the 10.1 flag on the Gazette date). (2) The commentary ('General Notes', 406 characters) is cut off and prints no citation: 'Rule 10.9 applies to retainer agreements in which a lawyer makes an agreement with a client, and not a separate document between two parties that provides for the amount and manner of payment, such as a borrower agreeing to be responsible for a lender's solicitor-and-client costs (even though this does not derogate from the court's' followed by the page's running head 'PART 10 LAWYERS' CHARGES, RECOVERABLE COSTS OF LITIGATION, AND SANCTIONS'. It agrees with Book A's last paragraph ('Rule 10.9 only covers agreements between a lawyer and his or her client, not agreements between two non-lawyers') and its p.10-24 footnotes 1-2 (Manufacturers Life v. 423632 Alta. 2015 ABQB 566; CIBC Mtge. v. Ulrich 2015 ABQB 445, both foreclosure costs, 'the lender's security'); the same sentences are in the 6.47 note. The passage is kept as printed (flagged); its source case is not named in Book C."},
    "10.8": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): it equals the official words except for the bracket labels '[Contingency fee agreement requirements]' after 'rule 10.7(1) to (4), (6) and (7)' and '[Payment for lawyer's services and contents of lawyer's account]' after 'rule 10.2' (the official titles of 10.7 and 10.2), printed in the text.", 'citation_names': {'2005 ABQB 352': 'Sonnenberg v. Schumacher & Associates', '2015 ABQB 682': 'Niam v. Silverberg', '2023 ABKB 321': 'Mikisew Cree First Nation v. Rath & Co.'}, 'commentary_flag': "(1) The commentary ('General Principles', 1,522 characters as built) is damaged and cut off: 'compensation is calculated on a basis. quantum meruit' (the words 'quantum meruit' are displaced to after 'basis.'); 'cited in , [2015] A.J. No. 1161, 2015 ABQB 682 at para. 124 ... Niam v. Silverberg' (the case name is printed after the citation); 'a lack of proof of both time and manner of service on the client ( , no proof of service)' and 'The defects of a i.e. contingency agreement' (the 'i.e.' is displaced); 'but see, by contrary example on particular facts, , [2023] Mikisew Cree First Nation v. Rath & Co. A.J. No. 550, 2023 ABKB 321' (name after the citation); the text ends 'A fully informed client may be able to effectively' followed by the heading of the next Subdivision ('Subdivision 4: RIGHT OF REVIEW'). The built citation records had given 2015 ABQB 682 the name 'Sonnenberg v. Schumacher' and 2023 ABKB 321 'Mikisew Cree First Nation v. Rath'; repaired from the printed text (Niam v. Silverberg; Mikisew Cree First Nation v. Rath & Co.). (2) Read against Book B: the quantum meruit statement, the client's address not being fatal while lack of proof of the time and manner of service is (Sonnenberg), 'construed strictly against the lawyer' (Sonnenberg para 38, quoted in Book B and in Book B's 10.7 commentary), 'only relaxed in exceptional cases' (Niam para 123, quoted in Book B) and 'only in the rarest circumstances ... written ... filed ... fully informed client may be able to effectively [waive]' (Veit J. in Leffler v. Collins, quoted in Niam para 122 in Book B) all agree; the Mikisew para 81 'contrary example' agrees with Book A's p.10-18 fn 4 (paras 81-95). Sonnenberg para 24 and Niam para 124 (the pinpoints in Book C's first two sentences) are not among Book B's quotations. Kept as printed, flagged."},
    "10.7": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): it stops in (2)(e)(ii) after 'detailing the disbursements and other charges that are included' and goes straight to '(3) The contingency fee agreement must be witnessed ...', so (2)(e)(ii) to (h) are missing; in (4) the number '10' ('within 10 days') is missing and this citation stands in its place: 'Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs LLP, [2014] A.J. No. 62, 2014 ABQB 34 at para. 50 (Alta. Q.B.).'; in (5) the number '5' ('within 5 days') is missing and this citation stands in its place: 'Rath & Co. v. Sweetgrass First Nation, [2013] A.J. No. 268, 2013 ABQB 165 at para. 77 (Alta. Q.B.), revd but not on principles of law, [2014] A.J. No. 1392, 2014 ABCA 426 (Alta. C.A.), leave to appeal refused [2015] S.C.C.A. No. 67 (S.C.C.).'; (1), (2)(a)-(e)(i) and (3)-(8) otherwise equal the official words. The amendment note '[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.7 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021); Alta. Reg. 128/2015, s. 8]' agrees with the official 'AR 124/2010 s10.7;128/2015' (it is split across two lines by a stray '*').", 'drop_citations': "Both citations stand where a number is lost in Book C's rule text and are not 10.7 authorities as printed here: Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs LLP 2014 ABQB 34 para 50 stands where '10' is lost in 10.7(4) ('within [10] days'), and Book B's quotation of Steinke in its 10.9 commentary puts para 50 on the review officer's ethical obligation, not on service; Rath & Co. v. Sweetgrass First Nation 2013 ABQB 165 para 77 stands where '5' is lost in 10.7(5) ('within [5] days'), and Book B's 10.2 commentary (part 5) gives paras 77-78 as the common-law factors under 10.2(1). Both are dropped as displaced (they carry no commentary of their own in this entry); the built records had given the first a style of cause made of rule text ('The client must be served ... Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs LLP') and the other two the broken name 'Co. v. Sweetgrass First Nation'.", 'drop_note_variant': "Book C's copy of the Information Note ('The transitional provisions of these rules contain rules protecting former contingency fee agreements entered into before these rules come into force. See PART 10 LAWYERS' CHARGES, RECOVERABLE COSTS OF LITIGATION, AND SANCTIONS') has the same words as Book A's but is cut off after 'See' by the page's running head ('Part 15 [Transitional Provisions and Coming Into Force]' is missing); Book A's copy is kept."},
    "10.6": {'drop_c_note': "Book C's copy of the Information Note is dropped: it has the same words as Book A's ('The rules about self-representing are in rule 2.28 [Change in lawyer of record or self representation]') with the hyphen of 'self-representation' lost, and the heading 'Subdivision 3: CONTINGENCY FEE AGREEMENTS' (the Subdivision that begins at 10.7) printed after it."},
    "10.5": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): (1) and (3) are printed, but (2) stops after '(b) commission,' - subparagraphs (2)(c) percentage, (d) salary and (e) an hourly rate are missing - and (3) has the bracket label '[Payment for lawyer's services and contents of lawyer's account]' (the official title of 10.2) after 'rule 10.2'; the words printed otherwise equal the official text.", 'citation_names': {'2014 ABCA 268': 'Samson Cree Nation v. O’Reilly & Associés'}, 'commentary_flag': "(1) The commentary ('General Principles', 2,087 characters as built) is cut off at the end ('The court must hold the lawyer and the client to promises made in a retainer') and has printing defects: the footnote number '22' is fused to 'rule 10.5.22'; the statute title is displaced ('is made within the meaning of the , when the appointment Limitations Act for assessment is taken out'); 'tentative- ness' is a line-break hyphen; the last case name is incomplete ('This was reiterated in Attila Dogan Construction and Installation Co. Inc. v. Bennett' with no citation - Book A cites Attila Dogan Constr. only as a party to 'Attila Dogan Constr. & Installation Co. v. AMEC Americas 2011 ABQB 794' (p.10-82, line 4308, 10.31 note) and 'AMEC Foster Wheeler etc. v. Attila Dogan Constr. etc. 2016 ABQB 305' (p.10-165, line 8921, 10.53 note), and Book B's 10.10 commentary cites 'Attila' (Wittmann C.J., para 35); no source names a decision 'v. Bennett'). The sentence 'The court must hold the lawyer and the client to promises made in a retainer' is the third principle of Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs 2014 ABQB 34 as Book B quotes it in its 10.9 commentary ('a court must hold the lawyer and the client to promises made in a retainer agreement'). (2) Read against the official text: 'A lawyer seeking to collect on a contingency fee who has not complied with rule 10.7 cannot obtain assistance from rule 10.5' agrees in substance with 10.8 (a lawyer who does not comply with 10.7(1)-(4), (6) and (7) is entitled only to charges determined under 10.2); 'like rule 10.7(7) (on contingency agreements) ... a future requirement that each account of a lawyer to a client contain a notice to the effect that a right to review is available' agrees with 10.7(7) (every account under a contingency fee agreement must state that a review officer may determine reasonableness); the suggested 'time limitations - including that it be brought within two years of the date of the account' is a proposal, and official 10.10(2) already bars review of a lawyer's charges one year after the account was sent; 'A claim for a remedial order ... is made within the meaning of the Limitations Act when the appointment for assessment is taken out. Any account pre-dating two years prior to this appointment is statute barred' agrees with Book A p.10-9 footnote 6 (Sharma: an appointment for taxation stops the limitation period running) and is a statement from Samson Cree, not in the Rules. The five bullets are attributed to Samson Cree Nation v. O'Reilly & Associes [2014] A.J. No. 904, 2014 ABCA 268 at paras 53, 81-82, 110, 165-169 (pinpoints found only here; Book A cites the decision without pinpoints); the printed name is displaced before the A.J. citation, so the build had given 2014 ABCA 268 no name - repaired from the printed text. The commentary is kept as printed and flagged."},
    "10.4": {'citation_names': {'2021 ABQB 988': 'Robertson LLP v. Pasco', '2021 ABQB 1024': 'M. (D.S.) v. S. (K.L.)'}, 'commentary_flag': "(1) Rule text equals the official text (EXACT_MATCH); the amendment note is in the standard form (see the 10.1 flag on the Gazette date). (2) The commentary ('General Principles', four paragraphs, 1,909 characters as built) was read in full against the official text, Book A and Book B: 'a charging order under rule 10.4 ... may only be made, pursuant to subrule (2), if two requirements are satisfied' agrees with 10.4(2)(a)-(b) ('First, the lawyer must establish that the fees are unlikely to be paid without the order. Second, the property to be charged must be associated with the lawyer's work and that work must result in recovery or preservation of the property'); the quotation 'The purpose of r 10.4(2) would be best met by permitting the 10.4(2)(a) requirement to be established at the time of bringing the application for a charging order, or within a reasonable time subsequently' is word for word paragraph [51] of Paragon Capital Corp. v. Starke Dominion 2020 ABCA 216 as Book B quotes it in its part 2; the 10.4(5) paragraph (unfairness from granting, not from refusing) matches Book B's part 12 (Paragon [52]-[53]) and Book A's footnote 6 on p.10-9 ('Paragon v. Starke, supra (¶ 53)'); the paragraph on excessive delay (M. (D.S.) v. S. (K.L.) 2021 ABQB 1024 para 25) agrees with Book A p.10-10 footnote 1 ('Delay in moving is a ground to deny a charging order for unpaid fees ... D. S. M. v. K. L. S. 2021 ABQB 1024') and with Book B's Merchant Law Group passage on laches; the priority paragraph ('a contextual analysis, it is not always that they take such priority') agrees with Book A's last note paragraph ('does not always have priority over other registered interests') and its footnote 5 (Robertson LLP v. Pasco 2021 ABQB 988, paras 11-21). (3) Printing defects: the last sentence prints its citation with the case name displaced after it - 'see also , [2021] A.J. No. 1758, 2021 ABQB 988 at para. 13 (Alta. Q.B.). Robertson LLP v. Pasco RETAINER GREEMENTS A' - and ends with a fragment of the next Subdivision's heading ('RETAINER AGREEMENTS', letters lost); in the delay paragraph the name 'M. (D.S.) v. S. (K.L.)' is printed before '[2021] A.J. No. 1749, 2021 ABQB 1024'. The built citation records were repaired from the printed text (2021 ABQB 988 = Robertson LLP v. Pasco; 2021 ABQB 1024 = M. (D.S.) v. S. (K.L.)); the build had given the first the name of the previous case (Paragon) and the second no name. Paragon is cited at para. 51, paras 53-54 and, in the priority paragraph, without a pinpoint."},
    "10.2": {'commentary_flag': '(1) Rule text equals the official text (EXACT_MATCH). (2) The commentary (heading \'General Principles\', 347 characters, no citation printed) is garbled and cut off: \'The default method used to assess legal accounts where no retainer agreement is found is rule 10.2.1\' (the \'1\' after \'rule 10.2.\' is a footnote number whose text is not printed) \'Rule 10.2(1) introduces a reasonableness measure shaped by four specific but hard-to- similar conclusions as to what is a reasonable amount. The value of this process is not PART 10 LAWYERS\' CHARGES, RECOVERABLE COSTS OF LITIGATION, AND SANCTIONS\' - words are missing between \'hard-to-\' and \'similar\', and the sentence ends at \'not\' followed by the page\'s running head. The same words are in Book B\'s 10.9 commentary (part 6), quoting Steinke v. Hajduk Gibbs LLP 2014 ABQB 34 (para 51 by Book B\'s numbering): \'Rule 10.2(1) introduces a reasonableness measure shaped by four specific but hard-to-apply factors ("(a) the nature, importance and urgency of the matter, (b) the client\'s circumstances, ... (d) the manner in which the services are performed, (e) the skill, work and responsibility involved") and one omnibus and equally abstract factor ... It is safe to say that adjudicators asked to apply these factors are seldom likely to come up with similar conclusions as to what is a reasonable amount. In other words, the value of this process is not predictability and certainty.\' so the passage\'s \'four specific\' factors are the ones it lists, (a), (b), (d) and (e), with an ellipsis where (c) stands and \'any other factor\' (f) as the omnibus factor; 10.2(1) itself has six lettered factors. The first sentence agrees with Book A (\'Rule 10.2(1) is only a default mode, operating in absence of different contractual provisions\') and with Book B\'s part 3 (the Rule 613 factors apply \'absent any agreement as to fees\'). The passage is kept as printed (flagged) because Book C prints no source for it.', 'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '*[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.2 effective November 1, 2010 Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021]*' - the parentheses around the Gazette entry that other Book C notes have are missing; 'Alta. Reg. 124/2010' and 'November 1, 2010' agree with the official history (AR 124/2010, no amending regulation); the Gazette date 'May 15, 2021' is the one Book C prints throughout Part 10 (see the 10.1 flag) and was not checked."},
    "10.1": {'drop_rule_text': "Book C's rule text is dropped (official, Book A and Book B carry the whole text): it stops after '(ii) sufficient experience in the practice of law, and who is desig- nated as a review officer by' (with the hyphenated 'desig- nated'), so subparagraphs (iii) and (iv) of (b) are missing; what is printed equals the official words (the official (i)-(ii) are printed inline). The Subdivision heading 'Subdivision 1: LAWYERS' CHARGES' printed after the amendment note is the heading of Subdivision 1, which begins at 10.2 in the official text.", 'amendment_note_flag': "Book C prints '[Alta. Reg. 124/2010, r. 10.1 effective November 1, 2010 (Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021)]': 'Alta. Reg. 124/2010' and 'November 1, 2010' agree with the official history (AR 124/2010, no amending regulation). The Gazette date 'May 15, 2021' is printed on Book C's Part 10 entries throughout (the four Part 10 files, 441-520, have 'Alta. Gaz. May 15, 2021' on 100 lines and 'August 14, 2010' only at rules 11.1-11.8), while its Part 3 entries print 'August 14, 2010'; the official text gives no Gazette date, so the printed date is kept as printed and was not checked."},
}


def dedupe(packet: dict) -> None:
    """Remove redundancy without losing information: every dropped value is identical (after the
    documented normalization) to a value kept elsewhere, and its hash/locator stays in place."""
    log = []
    for s in packet["subrules"]:
        r, src, comp = s["rule"], s["sources"], s["comparison_vs_official"]
        # 1. book operative text identical to official -> keep hash + status only
        for cid in ("BOOK_A", "BOOK_B", "BOOK_C"):
            rec = src.get(cid)
            if rec and comp[cid]["status"] == "EXACT_MATCH":
                rec["operative_text_raw"] = None
                rec["operative_text_note"] = f"same as official operative text ({comp[cid]['status']}); see operative_text_sha256"
                log.append(f"{r} {cid}: operative text dropped ({comp[cid]['status']})")
        # 2. titles: keep official; list book variants only when wording (not case) differs
        t = s["title"]
        variants = {k: v for k, v in t.items() if k != "official" and v and norm_editorial(v) != norm_editorial(t["official"])}
        s["title"] = {"official": t["official"], "variants": variants}
        # 3. information notes: merge Book A / Book C duplicates
        notes = []
        a_note = src["BOOK_A"].pop("information_note", None) if src.get("BOOK_A") else None
        c_notes = src["BOOK_C"].pop("information_notes", []) if src.get("BOOK_C") else []
        if a_note:
            notes.append({"text": a_note, "carriers": ["BOOK_A"]})
        for cn in c_notes:
            hit = next((n for n in notes if _sim(n["text"], cn) >= 0.8), None)
            if hit:
                hit["carriers"].append("BOOK_C")
                if norm_strict(hit["text"]) != norm_strict(cn):
                    words = lambda x: set(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9.()]+", norm_strict(x).casefold()))
                    if words(cn) <= words(hit["text"]):
                        # same words, only scrambled: nothing new, so the garbled copy is not kept
                        hit.setdefault("carrier_defects", {})["BOOK_C"] = MANUAL_NOTE_FLAGS.get(
                            r, "garbled copy of the same note (word order/brackets); not retained")
                        log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C information note dropped: garbled duplicate, no new words")
                        continue
                    hit.setdefault("variant_text", {})["BOOK_C"] = cn
                log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C information note merged into BOOK_A copy")
            else:
                notes.append({"text": cn, "carriers": ["BOOK_C"]})
        s["information_notes"] = notes
        # 3b. Book C citation "context" is a window of the carrier text; drop it when that text is kept verbatim
        if src.get("BOOK_C"):
            kept = [src["BOOK_C"].get("operative_text_raw") or ""] + [c["text"] for c in src["BOOK_C"]["commentary"]]
            cits = list(src["BOOK_C"]["citations"]) + [x for c in src["BOOK_C"]["commentary"] for x in c.get("citations", [])]
            for cit in cits:
                ctx = cit.get("context")
                if ctx and any(ctx.strip() in k for k in kept):
                    cit.pop("context")
                    log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C citation context dropped ({cit.get('neutral_citation')}): verbatim in kept text")
        # 4. Book C commentary: drop per-item sentence splits (derived from the same text)
        if src.get("BOOK_C"):
            for grp in [src["BOOK_C"]["commentary"]] + [e["commentary"] for e in src["BOOK_C"]["misattributed_entries"]]:
                for c in grp:
                    if c.pop("sentences", None) is not None:
                        log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C commentary sentence split dropped")
        # 5. rule-by-rule manual curation of Book C (decided on manual review)
        cur = MANUAL_BOOK_C.get(r)
        if cur and src.get("BOOK_C"):
            c = src["BOOK_C"]
            if cur.get("drop_rule_text"):
                c["operative_text_raw"] = None
                c["operative_text_note"] = cur["drop_rule_text"]
                comp["BOOK_C"].pop("differences", None)
                log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C: rule text dropped (manual review)")
            if cur.get("rescue_misattributed"):
                for e in c.pop("misattributed_entries", []):
                    for item in e["commentary"]:
                        item["note"] = cur["rescue_misattributed"]
                        c["commentary"].append(item)
                    if e.get("parsed_title"):
                        for n in s["information_notes"]:
                            n["carriers"].append("BOOK_C")
                            n.setdefault("carrier_defects", {})["BOOK_C"] = "copy survives only as a garbled heading; not retained"
                log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C: misparsed entry folded into commentary; garbled heading dropped (manual review)")
            if cur.get("drop_note_variant"):
                for n in s["information_notes"]:
                    if n.get("variant_text", {}).pop("BOOK_C", None) is not None:
                        n.setdefault("carrier_defects", {})["BOOK_C"] = cur["drop_note_variant"]
                        if not n["variant_text"]:
                            n.pop("variant_text")
                        log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C information-note variant dropped (manual review)")
            if cur.get("note_flag"):
                for n in s["information_notes"]:
                    n["review_flag"] = cur["note_flag"]
            if cur.get("commentary_flag"):
                for cm in c["commentary"]:
                    cm["review_flag"] = cur["commentary_flag"]
            if cur.get("drop_c_note"):
                keep = []
                for n in s["information_notes"]:
                    if n["carriers"] == ["BOOK_C"]:
                        log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C information note dropped (manual review)")
                        continue
                    keep.append(n)
                for n in keep:
                    if "BOOK_A" in n["carriers"]:
                        n["carriers"].append("BOOK_C")
                        n.setdefault("carrier_defects", {})["BOOK_C"] = cur["drop_c_note"]
                s["information_notes"] = keep
            for cm in c["commentary"]:
                cm.setdefault("citations", []).extend(cur.get("add_commentary_citations", []))
            if cur.get("drop_commentary"):
                c["commentary"] = []
                c["commentary_note"] = cur["drop_commentary"]
                log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C: commentary dropped (manual review)")
            if cur.get("amendment_note_flag"):
                s["amendment_history"].setdefault("carrier_note_flags", {})["BOOK_C"] = cur["amendment_note_flag"]
            if cur.get("keep_citations_note"):
                c["citations_note"] = cur["keep_citations_note"]
            c["citations"].extend(cur.get("add_citations", []))
            if cur.get("drop_citations"):
                dropped = [x.get("neutral_citation") for x in c["citations"]]
                c["citations"] = []
                c["citations_note"] = cur["drop_citations"]
                log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C: displaced citations dropped {dropped} (manual review)")
            for nc_drop, why in cur.get("drop_one_citation", {}).items():
                c["citations"] = [x for x in c["citations"] if x.get("neutral_citation") != nc_drop]
                c.setdefault("dropped_citation_notes", {})[nc_drop] = why
                log.append(f"{r} BOOK_C: citation {nc_drop} dropped (manual review)")
            for cit in list(c["citations"]) + [x for cm in c["commentary"] for x in cm.get("citations", [])]:
                nc = cit.get("neutral_citation")
                if nc in cur.get("citation_notes", {}):
                    cit["note"] = cur["citation_notes"][nc]
                if nc in cur.get("citation_names", {}):
                    cit["style_of_cause"] = cur["citation_names"][nc]
        # 5a. amendment notes are kept once, in amendment_history.carrier_notes
        for cid in ("BOOK_B", "BOOK_C"):
            if (src.get(cid) or {}).pop("amendment_note_raw", None):
                log.append(f"{r} {cid}: amendment note moved to amendment_history.carrier_notes (was duplicated)")
        # 5b. manual drops of Book A / Book B raw text whose differences are editorial only
        for cid, note in MANUAL_TEXT_KEEP.get(r, {}).items():
            # raw text is NOT dropped: it holds the rule text interleaved with the whole printed note, which exists nowhere else in the packet
            rec = src.get(cid)
            if rec and rec.get("operative_text_raw"):
                rec["operative_text_note"] = note
                comp[cid]["review_note"] = note
                comp[cid].pop("differences", None)
                log.append(f"{r} {cid}: raw text KEPT (interleaved with the printed note); wording compared by eye (manual review)")
        for cid, note in MANUAL_TEXT_NOTES.get(r, {}).items():
            rec = src.get(cid)
            if rec and rec.get("operative_text_raw"):
                rec["operative_text_raw"] = None
                rec["operative_text_note"] = note
                comp[cid]["review_note"] = note
                comp[cid].pop("differences", None)
                log.append(f"{r} {cid}: raw text dropped, differences editorial only (manual review)")
        # 5c. Book C division heading vs official
        cdiv = (src.get("BOOK_C") or {}).get("division_heading")
        if cdiv and s["division"] and not cdiv.startswith(f"Division {s['division']['number']} "):
            src["BOOK_C"]["division_heading_flag"] = (f"wrong in Book C: rule {r} is in Division {s['division']['number']} "
                                                      f"({s['division']['heading']}) per the official text")
        if r in MANUAL_BOOK_A_COMMENTARY_FLAGS and src.get("BOOK_A"):
            src["BOOK_A"]["commentary_review_flag"] = MANUAL_BOOK_A_COMMENTARY_FLAGS[r]
        if r in MANUAL_SEE_ALSO:
            s["see_also"] = MANUAL_SEE_ALSO[r]
        # 6. manual flags on Book A footnotes
        for (pg, num), flag in MANUAL_BOOK_A_FOOTNOTE_FLAGS.get(r, {}).items():
            for fn in (src.get("BOOK_A") or {}).get("footnotes", []):
                if fn["page"] == pg and fn["number"] == num:
                    fn["review_flag"] = flag
    packet["dedupe_log"] = {"rule": "a value is dropped only when an equal value (under the normalization profile) is kept", "entries": log}


def main() -> int:
    official, off_meta = parse_official()
    a, a_meta = parse_book_a()
    b, b_meta = parse_book_b()
    c, c_meta = parse_book_c()

    pdf_hash = pdf_sha()
    a_year = latest_year(BOOK_A[0].read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    c_year = latest_year("\n".join(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8") for p in BOOK_C))
    last_part10_amend = max(int(y.split("/")[1]) for r in official.values() for y in r["amending_regulations"]) if any(
        r["amending_regulations"] for r in official.values()) else 2010

    registry = {
        "OFFICIAL": {
            "carrier_id": "OFFICIAL",
            "title": "Alberta Rules of Court, Alta. Reg. 124/2010 (Alberta King's Printer office consolidation)",
            "version": off_meta["consolidation"],
            "artifacts": [{"file": "Alberta rule of court.pdf", "sha256": pdf_hash, "branch": "main"},
                          {"file": OFFICIAL_TXT.name, "sha256": file_sha(OFFICIAL_TXT), "derived_from": "Alberta rule of court.pdf",
                           "method": "PyMuPDF page.get_text() (embedded text layer, no OCR)"}],
            "source_role": "FIRST_HAND_RULE_CARRIER",
            "origin_id": "ab-kings-printer-consolidation-2026-06-01",
            "permitted_use": "operative-text reconciliation anchor; official version/current-to closure",
        },
        "BOOK_A": {
            "carrier_id": "BOOK_A",
            "title": "Annotated rules text, Part 10 (publisher/title not stated in carrier; page style '10-N', 'Related Provisions', historical-derivation footnotes)",
            "version": f"unknown edition; latest Alberta case year cited in Part 10 = {a_year}",
            "artifacts": [{"file": BOOK_A[0].name, "sha256": file_sha(BOOK_A[0])}],
            "source_role": "ANNOTATED_RULES",
            "origin_id": "book-a-annotated-part10",
            "permitted_use": "corroboration; annotation (information notes, related provisions, commentary, footnotes)",
        },
        "BOOK_B": {
            "carrier_id": "BOOK_B",
            "title": "Alberta Rules of Court, The Honourable Justice Allan A. Fradsham (per carrier running header)",
            "version": b_meta.get("edition_header"),
            "artifacts": [{"file": p.name, "sha256": file_sha(p)} for p in BOOK_B],
            "source_role": "ANNOTATED_RULES",
            "origin_id": "book-b-fradsham",
            "permitted_use": "corroboration; commentary",
        },
        "BOOK_C": {
            "carrier_id": "BOOK_C",
            "title": "Annotated rules text, book pages 441-520 (publisher/title not stated in carrier; source files 441-460_revised.md ... 501-520_revised.md)",
            "version": f"unknown edition; latest Alberta case year cited = {c_year}",
            "artifacts": [{"file": p.name, "sha256": file_sha(p)} for p in BOOK_C],
            "source_role": "ANNOTATED_RULES",
            "origin_id": "book-c-annotated-pp441-520",
            "permitted_use": "corroboration; annotation (information notes, citations, commentary)",
        },
    }
    registry_sha = sha_text(json.dumps(registry, sort_keys=True))

    def version_identity(cid: str) -> tuple[str, str]:
        floor = {"BOOK_A": a_year, "BOOK_B": int(b_meta["edition_year"]) if b_meta.get("edition_year") else None, "BOOK_C": c_year}[cid]
        if floor and floor > last_part10_amend:
            return "SAME_VERSION_PROVEN", (f"carrier post-dates {floor} >= last Part 10 amendment year {last_part10_amend} "
                                           "per official amendment history; no Part 10 amendment after that date appears in the June 1, 2026 consolidation")
        return "VERSION_IDENTITY_UNRESOLVED", "carrier date cannot be placed after the last Part 10 amendment"

    books = {"BOOK_A": a, "BOOK_B": b, "BOOK_C": c}
    subrules, summary = [], {"EXACT_MATCH": 0, "NORMALIZATION_ONLY_DIFFERENCE": 0, "CARRIER_HAS_EXTRA_TEXT": 0,
                             "CARRIER_MISSING_TEXT": 0, "WORDING_DIFFERENCE": 0, "CARRIER_TEXT_MISSING": 0}
    gate_counts = {}
    for r in RULES:
        off = official[r]
        comps, carriers_gate, vis = {}, {}, {}
        for cid, data in books.items():
            rec = data.get(r)
            comps[cid] = compare(off["operative_text"], rec and rec["operative_text_raw"])
            summary[comps[cid]["status"]] += 1
            vi, basis = version_identity(cid)
            vis[cid] = {"result": vi, "basis": basis}
            comps[cid]["version_identity"] = vi
            if rec:
                carriers_gate[cid] = {
                    "carrier_id": cid,
                    "artifact_sha256": registry[cid]["artifacts"][0]["sha256"],
                    "text_sha256": rec["operative_text_sha256"],
                    "source_role": registry[cid]["source_role"],
                    "origin_id": registry[cid]["origin_id"],
                    "locator": rec["locator"],
                }
        carriers_gate["OFFICIAL"] = {
            "carrier_id": "OFFICIAL", "artifact_sha256": pdf_hash or file_sha(OFFICIAL_TXT),
            "text_sha256": off["operative_text_sha256"], "source_role": "FIRST_HAND_RULE_CARRIER",
            "origin_id": registry["OFFICIAL"]["origin_id"], "locator": off["locator"],
        }
        agree = all(comps[k]["status"] in ("EXACT_MATCH", "NORMALIZATION_ONLY_DIFFERENCE") for k in books)
        overall_vi = "SAME_VERSION_PROVEN" if all(v["result"] == "SAME_VERSION_PROVEN" for v in vis.values()) else "VERSION_IDENTITY_UNRESOLVED"
        if agree and overall_vi == "SAME_VERSION_PROVEN":
            result = "THREE_BOOK_SOURCE_RECONCILED"
        elif overall_vi == "SAME_VERSION_PROVEN" and off["operative_text"]:
            # the official carrier closes operative wording independently; book defects are preserved as provenance
            result = "SOURCE_CARRIER_DEFECT_INDEPENDENTLY_CLOSED"
        else:
            result = "THREE_BOOK_RECONCILIATION_HOLD"
        gate_counts[result] = gate_counts.get(result, 0) + 1
        gate = {
            "schema_version": "arc-three-book-gate-v1",
            "rule_identity": {"instrument": "Alta. Reg. 124/2010", "rule": r, "title_official": off["title"]},
            "three_book_mode": "OPTIONAL_CORROBORATION",
            "required_carriers": ["OFFICIAL"],
            "source_registry_sha256": registry_sha,
            "normalization_profile": {k: NORMALIZATION_PROFILE[k] for k in ("id", "version", "sha256")},
            "version_identity": overall_vi,
            "carrier_version_identity": vis,
            "pairwise_vs_official": {k: v["status"] for k, v in comps.items()},
            "result": result,
            "independent_origin_count": len({c["origin_id"] for c in carriers_gate.values()}),
            "carriers": carriers_gate,
        }
        gate["gate_artifact_sha256"] = sha_text(json.dumps(gate, sort_keys=True))
        subrules.append({
            "rule": r,
            "title": {"official": off["title"], "BOOK_A": a.get(r, {}).get("title"),
                      "BOOK_B": b.get(r, {}).get("title"), "BOOK_C": c.get(r, {}).get("title")},
            "division": off["division"],
            "subdivision": off.get("subdivision"),
            "operative_text": {
                "controlling": off["operative_text"],
                "controlling_carrier": "OFFICIAL",
                "sha256": off["operative_text_sha256"],
            },
            "amendment_history": amendment_check(off, a.get(r), b.get(r), c.get(r)),
            "sources": {
                "OFFICIAL": {"locator": off["locator"]},
                "BOOK_A": a.get(r),
                "BOOK_B": b.get(r),
                "BOOK_C": c.get(r),
            },
            "comparison_vs_official": comps,
            "three_book_gate": gate,
        })

    packet = {
        "schema_version": "arc-rule10-three-book-reconciliation-v1",
        "skill": "arc-rules-production-lifecycle",
        "mode": "SOURCE_RECONCILIATION",
        "write_status": "NO_WRITE (no Neo4j/LexGraph mutation; packet only)",
        "generated_utc": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
        "target": {"instrument": "Alberta Rules of Court, Alta. Reg. 124/2010", "part": 10, "rules": f"{RULES[0]}-{RULES[-1]}", "count": len(RULES)},
        "limits": [
            "Three-book agreement is not current-law certification; currency rests on the official consolidation's stated current-to date only.",
            "Book A and Book C titles/editions are not stated in their carriers; roles are inferred from content and recorded as such.",
            "Commentary and notes are copied as carried; no burdens, tests, or exceptions were added.",
            "Discrepancy status values are machine classifications for review, not adjudicated resolutions.",
        ],
        "source_registry": registry,
        "source_registry_sha256": registry_sha,
        "normalization_profile": NORMALIZATION_PROFILE,
        "denominators": {
            "source_closure_denominator": {"definition": "Alta. Reg. 124/2010 rules 10.1-10.55 in the June 1, 2026 consolidation", "count": len(RULES)},
            "pairwise_comparison_denominator": {"definition": "rules x book carriers (A,B,C) compared against OFFICIAL", "count": len(RULES) * 3},
        },
        "summary": {"pairwise_status_counts": summary, "gate_result_counts": gate_counts,
                    "last_part10_amendment_year": last_part10_amend},
        "part_level": {
            "official": off_meta,
            "BOOK_A": a_meta,
            "BOOK_B": b_meta,
            "BOOK_C": c_meta,
        },
        "subrules": subrules,
    }
    dedupe(packet)
    OUT_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    log = packet.pop("dedupe_log")
    subs = packet.pop("subrules")
    packet["files"] = [f"{x['rule']}.json" for x in subs]
    packet["dedupe_rule"] = log["rule"]
    (OUT_DIR / "_index.json").write_text(json.dumps(packet, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    for x in subs:
        x = {"index": "_index.json (source registry, normalization profile, denominators, part-level notes)", **x,
             "dedupe_log": [e for e in log["entries"] if e.split(" ")[0] == x["rule"]]}
        (OUT_DIR / f"{x['rule']}.json").write_text(json.dumps(x, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    print(json.dumps(packet["summary"], indent=2))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
